# Build-context exclusions (docs/plans/03-hardening-pass.md §D4).
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS EVEN THOUGH THE FINAL IMAGE IS DISTROLESS: each Dockerfile
# does `COPY . .` into its BUILD stage. Without this file, everything below
# gets uploaded to the daemon and baked into an intermediate layer — including
# secrets/, which holds real private keys on a developer's disk (gitignored,
# but gitignore has no bearing on a Docker build context). The final stage
# copies only the compiled binary, so those layers are not in the shipped
# image — but they exist in the local layer cache, and anyone who later adds a
# `COPY . .` to the runtime stage, or pushes an intermediate stage as a cache
# image, ships them. Excluding them here is the durable fix; relying on the
# final stage's discipline is not.
#
# It also makes builds meaningfully faster, since the context is uploaded to
# the daemon in full on every build.

# Real key material. The single most important line in this file.
secrets/

# Local environment files — these hold real credentials (Firebase service
# account, Gmail app password, LinkedIn secrets) and must never enter a build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control metadata: large, and nothing in the build reads it.
.git/
.gitignore

# Documentation. Nothing in either Dockerfile reads a .md file.
*.md

# Test and coverage output.
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.test
*.prof

# Editor/OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# The Dockerfiles themselves don't need to be inside the image they build.
cmd/*/Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
